      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Star youngster VERBICI (6) stretched his unbeaten record to eight when he raced parked but was too good at Listed level in Sydney last start to follow his easy Vicbred victory. Steps up from the mile but four of his wins have come at this distance range. The standing start is a new challenge but if he gets that right he is the one to beat. REGAL GALA (1) broke as a hot favourite last start but had been very reliable with a string of wins and placings prior. Has chased VERBICI home a few times already so it won't be easy to turn the tables but he won from the standing start here two back and that experience may prove a crucial advantage. PHOENIX REX (5) recovered from an early break for an easy win last start at Melton. Got the standing start wrong two back so those manners are some concern but he is capable. KYVALLEY DIXON (11) broke last start but had been consistent prior and came from the back row when winning the Vicbred 2F Final. With manners she could measure up to the boys.",
